- registry_updates is what removes placeholders downstream, so resolve aggressively: ALWAYS
  propose a name for the current Ghidra symbol, and for EACH unresolved symbol listed above
  propose a name whenever the call/usage context gives medium or high confidence
  (kind=function for FUN_/sub_, kind=global_var for DAT_/byte_/word_/dword_/qword_).

Output format — exactly three top-level blocks, in this order. Anything outside
these blocks (including markdown code fences) will be discarded.

  1. <named> ... </named>             the renamed C code; placeholders unchanged
  2. <naming_map> ... </naming_map>   human-readable rename log, one entry per line
  3. <registry_updates> ... </registry_updates>   JSON array

Tag pairing rules — most format errors come from violating these:
- </named> closes <named>. Never close <named> with </naming_map> or any other tag.
- </naming_map> closes <naming_map>. Never close it with </named>.
- Each opening tag appears exactly once. Never reopen a block after closing it.
- Do not nest blocks. Do not wrap any block in ```...``` fences.

